# Object-Oriented Library Manager

## Description

A C++ Object-Oriented Library Manager for managing books,
members, and loans.

## Features

- Add books
- List books
- Search book details
- Borrow books
- Return books
- Manage members
- Manage loans
- Import and export library records using CSV
- Input validation
- Error handling
- Automated tests

## OOP Concepts

- Classes and Objects
- Encapsulation
- Constructors
- Private and Public members
- Member functions
- Standard containers
- RAII

## Project Files

- `library_manager.h` - Book and Library class declarations
- `library_manager.cpp` - Book and Library implementations
- `storage.h` - Storage declarations
- `storage.cpp` - CSV file handling
- `member.h` - Member class declaration
- `member.cpp` - Member implementation
- `loan.h` - Loan class declaration
- `loan.cpp` - Loan implementation
- `main.cpp` - Main program
- `test_library.cpp` - Automated tests
- `library_records.csv` - Sample library records
- `CMakeLists.txt` - Build configuration

## Build

Using g++:

```bash
g++ main.cpp library_manager.cpp storage.cpp member.cpp loan.cpp -o library_manager
